course: dictionary
lesson: 11152
title: Clever tricks: the word wile
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A wile is a clever trick, or a charming way of getting someone to do what you want. The word is usually used in the plural, as wiles. Read the clues around it. «In the Road Runner cartoons the bird says "meep meep" and leaves Wile E.» Wile E. is always trying something sneaky, so wiles must be his tricks.
explain: Look for words that show a plan or a fooling. «Use all your wiles» means use every clever trick you know. If you swap in "tricks" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Wiles can be friendly as well as sneaky. A person can use charm and clever ways to win someone over. The context tells you whether the wiles are a trick to fool someone or a charming way to get what you want.
fact: A wile is a clever trick, and wiles means several of them.
fact: Wiles is usually used in the plural, as «wiles».
fact: «Wiles» means clever tricks or charming ways to persuade or fool someone.
fact: Wile E. Coyote is a cartoon character who uses many clever plans to catch the Road Runner.
fact: Old stories often describe the wiles of foxes, witches and villains.
exercise: Wile E. Coyote always has a new plan to catch the bird. What does wiles mean? | Loud noises and big crashes | Good manners at the dinner table | Sleepy, slow moves | *Clever tricks used to fool someone
exercise: «She used all her wiles to get a second slice of cake.» What does wiles mean here? | Long, sad songs | *Clever tricks and charming ways to get what she wanted | Plain words that said no
exercise: «The fox used his wiles to fool the hens.» Find and copy the noun that means clever tricks. | fox | used | hens | *wiles
test: The villain's charm and wiles fooled everyone in the town. What does wiles mean? | Heavy rain | Honest, plain speaking | *Clever tricks to fool people | Loud music
test: Which word means clever tricks or charming ways to fool someone? | Wild | Wind | Wire | *Wiles
exam: Ella says her little brother uses all his wiles to get sweets. What are his wiles? | Hard work at school | *Clever, charming tricks to get what he wants | Bad weather | Old clothes
